# The call is the one mention of the list in the text, and it runs once a turn. The turns of the loop are written out, and `apply` is not the built-in: the arm that calls as written may not make the list again, or each turn would hand over a new object where the program made one.
# A list that is made in the turn is a new one each turn, in plain as well.
# RUN: run-in-shell
# CHECK: other:a:2:0|same:changed:1:1|
# CHECK-NEXT: other:a:2:0|same:changed:1:1|
# CHECK-NEXT: other:a:2:0|same:changed:1:1|
# CHECK-NEXT: other:a:2:0|same:changed:1:1|
# CHECK-NEXT: other:a:2:0|other:a:2:0|
